<title>FRANCE: U.S. principal ex-Paris March aircargo destination.</title>
<headline>U.S. principal ex-Paris March aircargo destination.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in March 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in March 1997, with percentage change on March 1996 in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>1. United States  11,814 tonnes    (+5.4 percent)</p>
<p>2. Japan	     2,907 tonnes    (-7.5)</p>
<p>3. Hong Kong	 2,207 tonnes    (+7.9)</p>
<p>4. Germany	   2,143  tonnes  (+28.2)</p>
<p>5. UK		  1,949 tonnes   (+61.9)</p>
<p>6. Canada	    1,871 tonnes    (+0.2)</p>
<p>7. Brazil	    1,551 tonnes   (+13.2)</p>
<p>8. U.A.E.	    1,479 tonnes   (+10.7)</p>
<p>9. Mexico	    1,223 tonnes   (+18.2)</p>
<p>10. India	    1,197 tonnes    (-8.6)</p>
<p>11. Singapore	1,104 tonnes   (+64.1)</p>
<p>12. Saudi Arabia   1,030 tonnes   (-11.3)</p>
<p>13. Fr.W.Indies    1,013 tonnes   (-16.6)</p>
<p>14. Reunion	    815 tonnes   (-13.5)</p>
<p>15. Thailand	   807 tonnes   (+14.0)</p>
<p>16. Lebanon	    802 tonnes   (+13.1)</p>
<p>17. Egypt		733 tonnes    (-7.5)</p>
<p>18. Italy		665 tonnes   (-23.4)</p>
<p>19. Korea		642 tonnes    (-9.5)</p>
<p>20. China		502 tonnes   (-32.3)</p>
<p>March 1997 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 52,237 tonnes, up 0.8 percent on the same month in 1996, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
